Black's bishop on f8 is slightly short of defenders. Only Black's king on e8 and the rook on h8 keep it defended.

White has the superior minor pieces. Black's f8-bishop is a problem piece, hemmed in by its own pawns on c5 and d6. Meanwhile, White is slightly ahead on material. White is a pawn up.
